4340/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/state.json" "file_sha256" "e88b9d7950c3b7315955639dad412b561335e47da1926578f4da365795c6c21e" "basis" 763 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11568" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/state.json" "file_sha256" "e88b9d7950c3b7315955639dad412b561335e47da1926578f4da365795c6c21e" "basis" 763 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $AB$ and $BA,$ if \n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-4401.json" "file_sha256" "130a347366d6cc521a98a2525ae45705a5425abe282fba7ea5ced39e91e8c62c" "basis" 763 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot (-1) & 1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2 \\\\ -5\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1) & -5\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1 \\\\ -1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-5) & -1\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ -11 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** Notice that \n\n$$\nAB \\neq BA.\n$$\n\nMatrix multiplication is not **commutative**, meaning that when we switch the order of multiplication, we often get a different result (like we did in this example)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-4401.json" "file_sha256" "130a347366d6cc521a98a2525ae45705a5425abe282fba7ea5ced39e91e8c62c" "basis" 763 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $Z=XY.$ What is the value of $z_{32}$, if\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-5255.json" "file_sha256" "f9fdf6f4e7ee28b503083867424e562abff332d2f4d00fae68a62694cb970849" "basis" 763 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $X$ by the $2$nd column in $Y$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}_{32} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-1+8-6 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-5255.json" "file_sha256" "f9fdf6f4e7ee28b503083867424e562abff332d2f4d00fae68a62694cb970849" "basis" 763 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $AB$, if \n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-4402.json" "file_sha256" "ddcefab4accf9604577626e3f787ba05bcc6fb0b27771bf772dbfcd52866f4e0" "basis" 763 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0+0-9 & -6+0-3 & 4+0+6 \\\\ 0-1+6 & 9+2+2 & -6-4-4 \\\\ 0+0+3 & -6+0+1 & 4+0-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 13 & -14 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/example-4402.json" "file_sha256" "ddcefab4accf9604577626e3f787ba05bcc6fb0b27771bf772dbfcd52866f4e0" "basis" 763 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974340/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-1018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem